WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.600
Plot the pressure inside the left ventricle against its volume.

2
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.520
Each heartbeat then draws a closed loop.

3
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.320
This is a model adult ventricle at rest, with made-up numbers.

4
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.160
It has four corners, and an area inside.

5
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.940
When the arteries tighten, which corner moves?

6
00:00:19.983 --> 00:00:21.783
The beat runs counterclockwise.

7
00:00:22.263 --> 00:00:24.263
At the bottom right, the mitral valve closes.

8
00:00:24.903 --> 00:00:29.063
That volume is the end-diastolic volume, 125 mL.

9
00:00:29.723 --> 00:00:31.663
Pressure now rises with the volume fixed.

10
00:00:32.183 --> 00:00:36.743
At about 80 mmHg, the aortic valve opens and the ventricle ejects.

11
00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.323
At the top left, the aortic valve closes.

12
00:00:39.923 --> 00:00:46.063
That volume is the end-systolic volume, 45 mL, at 120 mmHg.

13
00:00:46.863 --> 00:00:48.983
Pressure then falls with the volume fixed.

14
00:00:48.983 --> 00:00:52.183
The mitral valve opens, and the ventricle fills.

15
00:00:53.717 --> 00:00:55.937
The width of the loop is the stroke volume.

16
00:00:56.637 --> 00:01:00.137
125 minus 45 is 80 mL.

17
00:01:00.797 --> 00:01:05.657
Divide 80 by 125, and the ejection fraction is 64 percent.

18
00:01:06.377 --> 00:01:08.997
The area inside the loop is the stroke work of the beat.

19
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.480
The top left corner lies on a line, the end-systolic pressure-volume relation.

20
00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:19.480
Its slope, Ees, is a relatively load-independent index of contractility.

21
00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:26.140
Here Ees is 3 mmHg per mL, and the line meets the volume axis at 5 mL.

22
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.280
A second line starts at the end-diastolic volume and runs to the corner.

23
00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:35.640
Its steepness is the effective arterial elastance, Ea, here 1.5.

24
00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.040
The corner sits where the two lines meet.

25
00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:43.530
Now tighten the arteries, and hold filling and contractility fixed.

26
00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:47.610
In the model, arteriolar constriction raises Ea to 2.

27
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:51.330
The steeper line meets the same end-systolic line higher up.

28
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.390
End-systolic pressure rises to 144 mmHg.

29
00:01:55.390 --> 00:01:59.610
End-systolic volume rises to 53 mL.

30
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.890
Stroke volume falls to 72.

31
00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:05.870
Ejection fraction falls to 57.6 percent.

32
00:02:06.733 --> 00:02:10.673
Filling and contractility did not change, yet ejection fraction fell.

33
00:02:11.353 --> 00:02:14.613
So ejection fraction can change with no change in contractility.

34
00:02:15.153 --> 00:02:16.273
Go back to the first loop.

35
00:02:17.013 --> 00:02:20.813
Raise filling to 140 mL, and the corner slides up the same line.

36
00:02:21.653 --> 00:02:22.953
Stroke volume rises to 90.

37
00:02:23.693 --> 00:02:28.453
Now return filling to 125, and raise Ees to 4.5.

38
00:02:28.933 --> 00:02:32.693
The line steepens, and end-systolic volume falls to 35.

39
00:02:33.293 --> 00:02:38.693
The rule to keep: preload, afterload and contractility each change the loop in a

40
00:02:38.693 --> 00:02:39.213
different way.
